<%- include('partials/head') %>
<main id="main">
  <section class="pageHero">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="kicker"><%= eyebrow %></span>
      <h1><%= heading %></h1>
      <p><%= intro %></p>
      <div class="heroPills"><span>GBP pricing</span><span>Availability checked before payment</span><span>Support by VPN4U</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="pricingGrid <%= type==='vps'?'pricingGridVps':'' %>">
        <% products.forEach(function(p){ %>
          <article class="priceCard <%= p.featured?'featured':'' %>">
            <% if(p.featured){ %><div class="popular">Popular choice</div><% } %>
            <div class="priceTop"><div><span class="tag"><%= type==='dedicated'?'Dedicated':type==='vpn'?'VPN':'VPS' %></span><h2><%= p.name %></h2></div><div class="price"><span>£</span><strong><%= Number(p.price).toFixed(Number(p.price)%1?2:0) %></strong><small>/<%= p.term||'month' %></small></div></div>
            <p><%= p.description %></p>
            <div class="specList">
              <% if(p.cpu){ %><div><span>Compute</span><strong><%= p.cpu %></strong></div><% } %>
              <% if(p.cores){ %><div><span>Cores</span><strong><%= p.cores %></strong></div><% } %>
              <% if(p.ram){ %><div><span>Memory</span><strong><%= p.ram %></strong></div><% } %>
              <% if(p.storage){ %><div><span>Storage</span><strong><%= p.storage %></strong></div><% } %>
              <% if(p.traffic){ %><div><span>Traffic</span><strong><%= p.traffic %></strong></div><% } %>
              <% if(p.network){ %><div><span>Network</span><strong><%= p.network %></strong></div><% } %>
              <% if(p.ip){ %><div><span>Addressing</span><strong><%= p.ip %></strong></div><% } %>
              <% if(p.devices){ %><div><span>Devices</span><strong><%= p.devices %></strong></div><% } %>
              <% if(p.protocols){ %><div><span>Protocols</span><strong><%= p.protocols %></strong></div><% } %>
              <% if(p.bandwidth){ %><div><span>Usage</span><strong><%= p.bandwidth %></strong></div><% } %>
              <% if(p.regions){ %><div><span>Locations</span><strong><%= p.regions %></strong></div><% } %>
            </div>
            <% if(p.setup){ %><div class="setupFee">One-time setup from £<%= Number(p.setup).toFixed(0) %></div><% } %>
            <a class="button full" href="/order/<%= type %>/<%= p.slug %>">Order / check availability</a>
          </article>
        <% }) %>
      </div>
      <div class="notice"><strong>Availability and pricing</strong><p><%= note %> Published prices are indicative retail prices in GBP and may change before an order is accepted. Taxes, licensing and optional add-ons may apply. VPN4U confirms the material configuration and final amount before requesting payment.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <% if(type==='vps'){ %>
    <section class="section sectionMuted"><div class="container"><div class="sectionHead"><div><span class="kicker">What is included</span><h2>Virtual infrastructure without unnecessary extras.</h2></div><p>Standard VPS plans are intended as self-managed compute for common internet and application workloads.</p></div><div class="featureGrid">
      <article><h3>NVMe storage</h3><p>Fast local storage for operating systems, applications, databases and general production workloads.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Public networking</h3><p>IPv4 and IPv6 connectivity is listed on the standard plans, with regional network availability confirmed at ordering.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Administrative access</h3><p>VPS products are intended to provide operating-system administrator access unless an accepted order states otherwise.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Global region options</h3><p>VPS capacity can be available across Europe, North America and Asia-Pacific, subject to live platform capacity.</p></article>
    </div></div></section>
    <section class="section"><div class="container split"><div><span class="kicker">Common uses</span><h2>Flexible compute for services you control.</h2><p>VPS plans are suited to websites, APIs, development environments, container workloads, small databases, monitoring systems, private applications and self-hosted services.</p><p>Standard VPS hosting is primarily an infrastructure service. Unless a managed service is explicitly included, the customer remains responsible for operating-system configuration, software, security updates, application administration and backups.</p></div><div class="factPanel"><div><span>Entry workloads</span><strong>Websites & development</strong><small>Start with lower-resource plans and scale when the application grows.</small></div><div><span>Production workloads</span><strong>Apps, APIs & databases</strong><small>Balanced plans add memory and compute for busier services.</small></div><div><span>Larger deployments</span><strong>Containers & multi-service hosts</strong><small>Higher tiers provide additional headroom for dense application stacks.</small></div></div></div></section>
    <section class="section sectionMuted"><div class="container faqList"><div class="sectionHead"><div><span class="kicker">VPS FAQ</span><h2>Before you order</h2></div></div><details open><summary>Is the VPS managed?</summary><p>Standard VPS plans are self-managed infrastructure. You manage the operating system, applications, security configuration and backups unless your accepted order explicitly includes managed support.</p></details><details><summary>Can I choose the operating system?</summary><p>Common Linux distributions are normally the simplest option. Ask sales if you need a particular image, Windows or other licensed software.</p></details><details><summary>Can I upgrade later?</summary><p>Upgrades may be possible depending on platform and regional capacity. Contact support before planning a change that depends on a specific upgrade path.</p></details><details><summary>Are backups included?</summary><p>Not unless explicitly stated in the accepted order. Maintain independent backups of important data.</p></details><details><summary>Can I request another location?</summary><p>Yes. Submit the preferred country or region and we will confirm whether an appropriate deployment location is available.</p></details></div></section>
  <% } %>

  <% if(type==='dedicated'){ %>
    <section class="section sectionMuted"><div class="container"><div class="sectionHead"><div><span class="kicker">Bare-metal service</span><h2>Physical compute with predictable resources.</h2></div><p>Dedicated servers are designed for workloads that benefit from exclusive CPU, memory and local storage resources.</p></div><div class="featureGrid">
      <article><h3>Dedicated hardware</h3><p>The physical server resources are allocated to the customer rather than shared as a normal VPS instance.</p></article>
      <article><h3>NVMe datacentre storage</h3><p>Standard configurations use fast NVMe storage, with larger or alternative storage reviewed as a custom requirement.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Full system control</h3><p>Dedicated products are intended to provide root or administrator-level operating-system control unless otherwise agreed.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Stock confirmed first</h3><p>Hardware availability changes. We verify the requested model, location and material specification before requesting payment.</p></article>
    </div></div></section>
    <section class="section"><div class="container split"><div><span class="kicker">Common uses</span><h2>For workloads that need consistent physical performance.</h2><p>Dedicated servers are suitable for larger databases, virtualisation hosts, busy web platforms, game services, build systems, data workloads and applications where predictable physical CPU or storage performance matters.</p><p>Standard dedicated servers are primarily unmanaged infrastructure. Customers should plan for operating-system administration, application security, monitoring and independent backups unless additional management is explicitly included.</p></div><div class="factPanel"><div><span>High-frequency compute</span><strong>Application & database hosts</strong><small>Modern single-socket systems for workloads that value strong per-core performance.</small></div><div><span>Memory-heavy workloads</span><strong>Virtualisation & data platforms</strong><small>Higher-memory configurations for dense guests, caches and analytical services.</small></div><div><span>Parallel workloads</span><strong>High-core-count compute</strong><small>EPYC-class options for sustained multi-threaded workloads and virtualisation density.</small></div></div></div></section>
    <section class="section sectionMuted"><div class="container faqList"><div class="sectionHead"><div><span class="kicker">Dedicated FAQ</span><h2>Before you reserve hardware</h2></div></div><details open><summary>Why do dedicated servers require an availability check?</summary><p>Specific CPU, storage and datacentre combinations are physical inventory. Stock can change, so VPN4U confirms availability before accepting payment.</p></details><details><summary>Are setup charges refundable?</summary><p>Physical allocation and setup costs may be non-refundable once provisioning has begun, except where required by law or where VPN4U cannot deliver the accepted service. See the Cancellation & Refund Policy.</p></details><details><summary>Can I request more RAM or storage?</summary><p>Often, yes, subject to compatible hardware and stock. Send the desired specification to sales for a custom review.</p></details><details><summary>Can I run virtual machines?</summary><p>The dedicated hardware can be suitable for virtualisation, but you are responsible for selecting appropriately licensed software and ensuring the chosen configuration meets your workload.</p></details><details><summary>Is a service-level guarantee included?</summary><p>No specific SLA should be assumed unless it is explicitly included in your accepted order.</p></details></div></section>
  <% } %>

  <% if(type==='vpn'){ %>
    <section class="section sectionMuted"><div class="container"><div class="sectionHead"><div><span class="kicker">Private connectivity</span><h2>Encrypted transport for everyday devices and small teams.</h2></div><p>VPN access is designed to protect traffic in transit and provide private network connectivity using established protocols.</p></div><div class="featureGrid">
      <article><h3>WireGuard</h3><p>A modern VPN protocol designed for efficient encrypted connectivity on supported devices and plans.</p></article>
      <article><h3>OpenVPN</h3><p>A mature protocol option for broad compatibility where supported by the selected service.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Multi-device plans</h3><p>Personal and business tiers list their device allowance so you can choose an appropriate plan.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Responsible privacy</h3><p>VPN4U does not market VPN access as a tool for illegal activity or make unsupported absolute anonymity claims.</p></article>
    </div></div></section>
    <section class="section"><div class="container split"><div><span class="kicker">What a VPN does</span><h2>Privacy in transit, not a promise of invisibility.</h2><p>A VPN encrypts traffic between your device and the VPN service and can change the public internet address seen by remote services. It does not make a device immune from malware, remove website tracking by itself or make unlawful activity lawful.</p><p>We deliberately avoid an absolute “zero logs” claim. Operational, security or account information may be processed where reasonably necessary to provide and protect the service, subject to our Privacy Policy and applicable law.</p></div><div class="factPanel"><div><span>Personal use</span><strong>Phones, laptops & tablets</strong><small>Encrypted connectivity for supported personal devices.</small></div><div><span>Small teams</span><strong>More device allowance</strong><small>Business plans provide additional device capacity and priority email support.</small></div><div><span>Usage policy</span><strong>Lawful use required</strong><small>VPN traffic remains subject to the Acceptable Use Policy.</small></div></div></div></section>
    <section class="section sectionMuted"><div class="container faqList"><div class="sectionHead"><div><span class="kicker">VPN FAQ</span><h2>Before you connect</h2></div></div><details open><summary>Does VPN4U guarantee anonymity?</summary><p>No. A VPN is one privacy and security layer. It does not prevent all forms of tracking or guarantee anonymity against every website, device, account or legal process.</p></details><details><summary>Do you have a fixed bandwidth cap?</summary><p>Current plans are advertised without a fixed bandwidth cap, subject to available network capacity, reasonable operation and the Acceptable Use Policy.</p></details><details><summary>Can I share one plan with unlimited devices?</summary><p>No. Each plan has a stated device allowance. Choose the business tier or contact sales if you need more devices.</p></details><details><summary>Can I use the VPN for abusive activity?</summary><p>No. Malware, attacks, spam, fraud and other prohibited uses remain prohibited regardless of whether a VPN is used.</p></details><details><summary>Which locations are available?</summary><p>Current plans describe multiple European and international exit locations. The exact active location list can change with service capacity.</p></details></div></section>
  <% } %>

  <section class="section"><div class="container cta"><div><span class="kicker">Need something different?</span><h2>Ask for a configuration review.</h2><p>Send your workload, preferred location and resource requirements. We can confirm whether a standard or custom option is appropriate.</p></div><a class="button" href="/contact">Contact sales</a></div></section>
</main>
<%- include('partials/footer') %>
